<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson says Q1 profit rises 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Ericsson says Q1 profit rises 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group Ericsson on Friday presented these earnings for the first three months of the year, ending March 31.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			   2,020  vs 1,549</p>
<p> Net sales				  30,705 vs 22,658</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	   1.40  vs 1.09</p>
<p> Order bookings			   39,213 vs 28,757</p>
<p> Cost of sales, other services	17,976 vs 13,219</p>
<p> Selling, R&amp;D, admin, general costs 10,621 vs  8,430</p>
<p> Operating profit			  2,477 vs  1,555</p>
<p> Financial income			    439 vs    398</p>
<p> Financial costs			     572 vs    346</p>
<p> Income after financial net	    2,344 vs  1,607</p>
<p> Associated interests			 78 vs    197</p>
<p> Minorities			   CHARGE 324 vs     58 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes					  660  vs    499</p>
<p> Net income				  1,360 vs  1,050</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that its mobile systems first quarter order bookings rose 22 percent and that its mobile phones and terminals net sales rose almost 100 percent.</p>
<p>The market had been expecting a first quarter profit of 1.99 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +468 700 1003</p>
</text>
